The experimental proposal package (/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite-worktrees/scene-decomposition-trials/docs/proposals/scene-decomposition-trials/README.md) covers three approaches:

- A: Independent components — separate the images, generate 3D models individually, and then assemble them.
- B: Composite modules — generate entire forest edge segments together, preserving their compositional relationships.
- C: Layered hybrid — use 3D for elements like rocks, while keeping plants as image layers.

The proposal standardizes the original artwork areas, ground, camera angles, and evaluation criteria. It first validates image segmentation and reassembly before proceeding to Tripo/Unity. It also specifies iteration limits, cost boundaries, stop conditions, and deliverables, and has completed the Luna feasibility review.
